  "containers": {
    "revolvedBowl": {
      "note": "innerProfile = (r, z) points on the inner wall, starting at the floor edge (horizontal tangent), then a cubic interpolation. The outer wall is the inner wall offset by wall along its normal; the rim is a semicircular arc. Foot: from the outer floor (rf, footH) -> (footR, footH) -> (footR-0.15, 0) -> (footR-0.15-footW, 0) -> (footR-0.3-footW, recess=min(0.25, footH/2)) -> axis. Revolve 360 degrees. The inner wall is the heightmap's initial floor: zIn(r)."
    },
    "roundedSlab": { "note": "Rounded rectangle extrusion. Top z = h. The heightmap is |x|<w/2-0.4 && |y|<d/2-0.4 -> h" }
  },

